  "sn39.1-15:1.1": "See notes on <a href='https://suttacentral.net/dn16/en/sujato#2.1.2'>DN 16:2.1.2</a>, <a href='https://suttacentral.net/sn47.13/en/sujato#1.1'>SN 47.13:1.1</a>, and <a href='https://suttacentral.net/sn47.14/en/sujato#1.1'>SN 47.14:1.1</a>. The Buddha taught there in <a href='https://suttacentral.net/mn34/en/sujato'>MN 34</a>. | The commentary requires the reading <i lang='pi' translate='no'>ukkacelā</i> (“cloth firebrand”) but its story is contrived. The variant <i lang='pi' translate='no'>ukkavelā</i> (“firebrand shore”) suggests there may have been a lighthouse there. ",
